I didn't change anything: you declined the write to `src/commands/global.options.js`, so I've stopped there. This is the change I'd make, in two files.

**`src/commands/global.options.js`**: a format option just for `accesslogs`, so `clever logs` doesn't start accepting `clf`. It follows how `envFormatOption` adds `shell`:

```js
export const accesslogsFormatOption = defineOption({
  name: 'format',
  schema: z.enum(['human', 'json', 'json-stream', 'clf']).default('human'),
  description: 'Output format',
  aliases: ['F'],
  placeholder: 'format',
});
```

**`src/commands/accesslogs/accesslogs.command.js`**: use that option instead of `logsFormatOption`, and add a formatter:

```js
const MONTHS = ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec'];

// Common Log Format: host ident authuser [date] "request" status bytes
function formatClf(log) {
  const { date, http, source, bytesOut } = log;
  const pad = (n) => String(n).padStart(2, '0');
  const clfDate = `${pad(date.getUTCDate())}/${MONTHS[date.getUTCMonth()]}/${date.getUTCFullYear()}`
    + `:${pad(date.getUTCHours())}:${pad(date.getUTCMinutes())}:${pad(date.getUTCSeconds())} +0000`;
  return `${source.ip} - - [${clfDate}] "${http.request.method} ${http.request.path}" ${http.response.statusCode} ${bytesOut ?? '-'}`;
}
```

In the `onLog` switch, a `case 'clf':` would skip logs without an `http` section (like `human` does) and print `Logger.println(formatClf(log))`. The "Beta testing phase" banner stays `human`-only, so the CLF output can be piped straight into tools like goaccess.

Two choices you might want to change:
- **No HTTP version in the request field.** The access log data doesn't include the protocol, so the field is `"GET /path"` rather than `"GET /path HTTP/1.1"`. Writing a fixed `HTTP/1.1` would be guessing.
- **Dates are in UTC (`+0000`)**, so the output is the same whatever the machine's timezone.

After that I'd run `npm run docs` to regenerate the options table and the skill reference. I'd also update the format list and add a CLF example in `docs/applications-deployment-lifecycle.md`, then run `npm run validate` and try `node bin/clever.js accesslogs -F clf --since 10m` on an app you name.

The repo history is a single snapshot commit, so I couldn't find the earlier CLF implementation to match its exact output. If you allow edits to `src/commands/` and `docs/`, I'll apply all of this.
